# Drafted by Gemini (R15 shack), edited.

~ arrive
set shack_met
quest withered_arm the_shack
cutscene dc_shack
Narrator: Green glass bottles bob in pairs across the black water, marking a sunken path of boards toward the lantern-lit shack.
cutscene dc_shack_2
Narrator: Up on the porch, a steel guitar rests across an empty rocking chair, humming a mournful tune all on its own.
cutscene end
-> END

~ guitar
Narrator: The damp cedar rocker creaks against the floorboards, and a single steel string rings out under no hand at all.
-> END

~ bay_bottle
Narrator: A lone bottle glows pale green in the weeds off the boards. Where one floats without its twin, something hungry sleeps in the silt.
-> END

~ parley
Narrator: Claws click down the iron spiral stair into the warm clutter of neon signs and bottled curios.
mister_crossroads [smile]: Step right in out of the damp, my friends. A humble sinner rarely gets the pleasure of the folks who rode the Ghostlight Express down the hill.
-> parley_menu

~ parley_menu
* Ask about Lady Adela's wedding ring. -> parley_adela
* [Insight DC 18] Watch how eagerly he mentions the Ghostlight Express. -> parley_keen | parley_keen_miss
* Ask to see his wares. -> wares
* Ask for passage to his riverboat. -> parley_passage
* [Intimidation DC 15] Threaten to take what we came for. -> parley_threat | parley_threat_miss
* Refuse any deal and leave. -> refuse
* Draw weapons and attack him. -> refuse

~ parley_adela
mister_crossroads [sly]: Ah, a lady of her breeding really ought to read the small print before signing. Still, she got her wish, and I keep her little gold band safe.
-> parley_menu

~ parley_keen
Narrator: His wide grin never wavers, yet his yellow eyes linger on your boots whenever the Ghostlight Express is named, hungry to know how you rode that iron train.
-> parley_menu

~ parley_keen_miss
Narrator: He stands with his hands folded over his waistcoat, nothing more than a polite host making small talk in a swamp.
-> parley_menu

~ parley_passage
mister_crossroads [smile]: Take any one thing from my shelves, a bargain or a simple curio tagged at three copper, and you are honoured guests aboard my boat. No catch at all.
-> parley_menu

~ parley_threat
mister_crossroads [smile]: Ha, now that is a warm welcome. Forgive an old sinner his chuckle, friends, but steel and bluster only spoil a pleasant evening among neighbours.
-> parley_menu

~ parley_threat_miss
mister_crossroads [smile]: Oh, splendid, it is always a genuine pleasure to be threatened by professionals. Do let me know when you are ready to talk business like civilised folk.
-> parley_menu

~ done_trading
mister_crossroads [smile]: Sold and sealed, my dear friends, as tidy as if you had bought the whole shop.
set crossroads_passage
give sinners_tag
set sinner_gone
mister_crossroads [smile]: Present that tag at the pier and join me aboard the Dead Man's Hand as my honoured guests.
Narrator: He snaps his clawed fingers and vanishes in a gout of sweet-smelling magenta fire.
-> END

~ refuse
mister_crossroads [weary]: Now look at the hour on my watch. You must excuse a busy man, friends, though I hate to leave you to the night air.
Narrator: He snaps his fingers and vanishes in a flash of magenta flame.
set crossroads_refused
set sinner_gone
Narrator: A wet roar shakes the pilings as a Bayou Beast splinters the front door inward, trailing six jinxed mosquitoes in its wake.
combat dc_shack_stalkers

~ steal_one
Narrator: The shack stands quiet in the lingering smoke, its shelves crowded with carved idols and stitched dolls, each neatly marked at three copper pieces.
* Take one tagged idol. -> steal_take
* Take nothing. -> END

~ steal_take
set crossroads_passage
give sinners_tag
Narrator: Three copper coins vanish from your purse to settle the price. You have your pass, though the riverboat will know you came as intruders.
-> END

# The wares (hand-written; see tools/content/crossroads_shop.py)

~ wares
mister_crossroads [smile]: Every bargain here costs a handshake and every trinket three copper, friend. One to a customer, and I am a stickler.
if flag.small_print_read
Narrator: Cora Beaudry's three tales sit in your head like a lamp: you can read the small print on every tag.
endif
* [if flag.sinner_deals < 4] A dark bargain, for a handshake -> bargains
* [if flag.sinner_deals < 4] A potion, tagged 3 CP -> potions
* [if flag.sinner_deals < 4] A curio or an idol, tagged 3 CP -> curios
* [if flag.sinner_deals >= 1] That is all of us -> done_trading
* Back to our talk -> parley_menu

~ bargains
mister_crossroads [sly]: A handshake is a small thing. It is binding once sealed, but small. Choose with your eyes open: each one shows its price.
* [if not flag.deal_bestial_awakening] Bestial Awakening -> take_bestial_awakening
* [if not flag.deal_call_of_the_lonely] Call of the Lonely -> take_call_of_the_lonely
* [if not flag.deal_collector_of_stories] Collector of Stories -> take_collector_of_stories
* [if not flag.deal_crooked_fortune] Crooked Fortune -> take_crooked_fortune
* [if not flag.deal_cult_of_personality] Cult of Personality -> take_cult_of_personality
* [if not flag.deal_hand_of_death] Hand of Death -> take_hand_of_death
* [if not flag.deal_might_of_the_old] Might of the Old -> take_might_of_the_old
* [if not flag.deal_self_serving_sacrifice] Self-Serving Sacrifice -> take_self_serving_sacrifice
* [if not flag.deal_shrouded_spirit] Shrouded Spirit -> take_shrouded_spirit
* [if not flag.deal_skin_of_coffin_nails] Skin of Coffin Nails -> take_skin_of_coffin_nails
* [if not flag.deal_stilled_hungers] Stilled Hungers -> take_stilled_hungers
* [if not flag.deal_unquenchable_fury] Unquenchable Fury -> take_unquenchable_fury
* [if not flag.deal_wings_of_whispers] Wings of Whispers -> take_wings_of_whispers
* Look at something else -> wares

~ take_bestial_awakening
Narrator: A paper tag on a string reads 3 CP, and under it, in small print: Polymorph, free once per Long Rest on yourself. The price: silvered weapons ignore your Resistances, and silver stops your healing.
mister_crossroads [smile]: A handshake, then. Who is it to be?
dark_gift bestial_awakening
if gift:bestial_awakening and not flag.deal_bestial_awakening and not flag.small_print_read
set deal_taken_blind
endif
if gift:bestial_awakening and not flag.deal_bestial_awakening
set deal_bestial_awakening
set sinner_deals += 1
Narrator: His hand is warm and dry, and something in your chest signs.
endif
-> wares

~ take_call_of_the_lonely
