~ take_the_bag
Narrator: A paper tag reads 3 CP. A satchel that holds 500 lb and weighs 5, with a Lurker in the Dark inside. It is cursed.
Narrator: The curse: Something lives in the bag. Each Long Rest, a 1 on a d6 means it slipped out in the night and caused mayhem close by. (Reference only; the game does not roll it yet.) It dies for good only to someone holding a child's toy, and then the bag is merely a bag.
mister_crossroads [smile]: Wrapped, and on the house, practically.
give the_bag
if not flag.ware_the_bag and not flag.small_print_read
set deal_taken_blind
endif
set ware_the_bag
set sinner_deals += 1
-> wares

~ take_green_ribbon
Narrator: A paper tag reads 3 CP. Worn at the neck, it adds 5 to your death saving throws. It is cursed.
Narrator: The curse: Anyone within 60 feet who is dying finds the dark pulling harder: they take a -1 penalty on death saves, and a worse one each time the ribbon is used. (Reference only; the penalty is not applied by the game yet.)
mister_crossroads [smile]: Wrapped, and on the house, practically.
give green_ribbon
